display A 17
sign a 1
sign b 12
sign c 14

# A swap opcode substitutes each item of its second operand for the
# item in the corresponding place in its third operand, so the two
# operands must contain the same number of items. Here the third
# operand is one item short, which should make the table compilation
# fail in a test.

swapcd dots abc 1,12
